# CP-67 MATRIX Engineering Standards

- Never bypass the 7-state escrow state engine for marketplace items.
- Geofenced functions must strictly reference the server-validated 50m boundaries.
- All pricing and values must use Nigerian Naira (NGN, ₦).
- When altering transaction files, never weaken, expose, or repurpose session handoff keys/tokens.
- Session handoff tokens must remain short-lived, single-use, opaque, and server-validated.
- Use official Material components from `@material/web` for UI primitives; do not use third-party kits (e.g. shadcn) or hand-rolled equivalents. Keep Tailwind for layout utilities only.
- Treat browser/device fingerprints as correlation signals, never authoritative identity proof.
- Physical meetup verification and escrow release must remain server-authoritative and mobile-gated.
- Never trust client-supplied GPS, EXIF, device type, transaction state, wallet balance, or PlugScore as authoritative.
- Persist offline transaction ownership with the authenticated user ID and reject/purge stale-user backlog before sync.
- Do not store Supabase access/refresh tokens or reusable credentials in QR codes, IndexedDB transaction payloads, URLs, or logs.
- Keep Edge Function health checks cheap and side-effect free; warm-up requests must use `x-health-check: true`.
- Prefer TypeScript-safe code, explicit return types for security-critical utilities, and no unsafe `as any` casts.
- Preserve existing RLS, rate limits, idempotency, escrow guards, duress protections, and payment verification when refactoring.
- Do not introduce live network/payment/database dependencies into structural CI regression tests.
- Before changing schema-dependent code, inspect `.ai-context/schema-dump.sql` and the relevant Supabase migrations.
- Run typecheck, build, tests, and security regression checks before declaring a change complete.
- Commit completed work to `main` without waiting to be asked. Split by concern, keep the repo imperative-mood, and push.

# Material 3 baseline

CRITICAL WORKSPACE RULE: Never write custom layout blocks, raw margins, or ad-hoc component styles. Always check the official imports in @material/web or @mui/material to see if a pre-built layout, container, or component exists first. Restrict designs completely to Material 3 design tokens.

- Colours resolve only through generated tokens (`var(--md-sys-color-*)`). Raw hex/`rgb()` literals in markup or component styles are a lint error.
- The palette is generated at runtime from the seed in `src/theme/theme.tokens.json` via `src/theme/themeEngine.ts`; never hand-edit token values in `src/index.css`.
- Full workspace rules live in `.clinerules`. The CP-67 security rules above always outrank styling requests.
